         <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Do not write the deconvoluted spectra to an SQLite database (.sqlite file). Leave it unchecked if TopPIC will search the spectra: its post mass matching, on by default, reads the MS/MS peaks from this database. The database also holds the MS1 peaks for the 3D view of TopMSV. Default: unchecked. (topfd -z, --no-sql)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
